        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Moscow Kremlin, Kremlin Arsenal, Cathedral of the Archangel, Cathedral Square, Moscow, Moskva River, Saint Basil's Cathedral, Red Square, Alexander Garden\n- People: Tsarevich Dmitry Alexeyevich of Russia\n- Topics: fortifications, burial sites\n\nFacts:\n- The Kremlin Arsenal was initially constructed in 1736 and has been rebuilt several times.\n- The Moscow Kremlin is a fortified complex in the heart of Moscow.\n- The Moscow Kremlin overlooks the Moskva River to the south, Saint Basil's Cathedral and Red Square to the east, and the Alexander Garden to the west.\n- The Cathedral of the Archangel is located in Cathedral Square within the Moscow Kremlin in Russia, between the Great Kremlin Palace and the Ivan the Great Bell Tower.\n- Tsarevich Dmitry Alexeyevich of Russia is buried in the Cathedral of the Archangel.",
